The cleanup function in the useEffect will not execute when editMode transitions from true to false. When editMode becomes false, the else block (line 18) calls `dnd.endDrag()` immediately, but the cleanup function from the previous effect run is not called until the component unmounts. This can lead to inconsistent DnD state. Consider restructuring the logic to ensure proper cleanup or remove the redundant `endDrag` call in the else block.
```suggestion
    if (!editMode) {
      return;
    }

    dnd.startDrag({ id: 'dashboard-layout', type: 'dashboard-widget', data: {} });
    return () => {
      dnd.endDrag();
    };
```

The type assertion `as Node` for `e.relatedTarget` could fail if `relatedTarget` is null. Consider adding a null check before the type assertion to prevent potential runtime errors.
```suggestion
    const relatedTarget = e.relatedTarget
    if (!relatedTarget) {
      setDropTargetIndex(null)
      return
    }
    if (!e.currentTarget.contains(relatedTarget as Node)) {
      setDropTargetIndex(null)
    }
```
